      "raw_extract_sha256": "de4bc9b7d7b5070b09a78b59e8aa752b9ac32f667e974fa910294824f08477d9",
      "readable_source_text": "Lemma 4.4 ( Uniform bound on the Krylov space). There is an absolute constant $C>0$ such that the following holds. Let $q\\geq 0$ satisfy $2q+1<d$ , let $g_{1},\\ldots,g_{q+1}$ be independent $N(0,I_{d})$ vectors, and let $\\mathcal{K}_{q}=\\mathcal{K}_{q}(g_{1},\\ldots,g_{q+1})$ . Define $\\tau_{d,q}=C\\left[(q+1)\\sqrt{\\frac{\\log d}{d}}+\\frac{(q+1)(q+1+\\log d)\\log d}{d}\\right].$ If $\\tau_{d,q}\\leq 1/2$ , then, with probability at least $0.99$ , $|u^{\\top}D_{n}u|\\leq 2\\tau_{d,q}\\|u\\|^{2}\\qquad\\text{for every }u\\in\\mathcal{K}_{q}.$"
    },
